2025-10-10 02:25:54,572 - evaluation_logger_Flights-32 - INFO - Final Response: ### Recommended Economy Class Flight Itinerary

Based on your travel plans (departing London on December 1, 2024, spending a week in Paris, then a week in Berlin, and returning to London on December 15, 2024), I've searched for the best multi-stop economy class flights. I prioritized the "BEST" option from the search results, which balances price, duration, and convenience. This itinerary uses EasyJet (U2) flights, all direct (no layovers), with early morning departures for optimal travel times. It's for 1 adult (you can scale pricing for your company by multiplying per person; contact the airline for group bookings).

**Total Estimated Price (per adult, in USD):** $202 (rounded; includes base fare of $146 + taxes/fees of $56). Prices are dynamic and may vary—book soon via EasyJet or a aggregator like Gotogate. No checked baggage is included (only 1 personal item per person, e.g., a small backpack up to 15x10x8 inches). Add-ons like hand luggage (~$102 per person round-trip) or seat selection (~$20–$30 per seat) are extra.

**Key Notes:**
- All flights are in Economy class on Airbus A320 aircraft (standard for EasyJet: 3-3 seating, no complimentary meals—light meals available for purchase ~$10).
- Baggage: Personal item only (no hand luggage). Checked bags start at ~$40 each way.
- Carbon footprint: ~236 kg CO2 per person (11% above average for this route).
- ATOL protection: Not applicable (non-UK operator for full trip).
- For your company: Assume multiple adults—total cost scales linearly. No child/infant details provided, so priced for adults only.

#### Flight 1: London (LTN - Luton Airport) to Paris (CDG - Charles de Gaulle Airport)
- **Date:** December 1, 2024
- **Flight Number:** U2 4640 (operated and marketed by EasyJet)
- **Departure:** 08:00 AM from LTN (London Luton Airport, ~35 miles north of central London; allow 1–1.5 hours travel time)
- **Arrival:** 10:20 AM at CDG (Paris Charles de Gaulle, ~15 miles northeast of central Paris; RER train to city center ~30 mins)
- **Duration:** 1 hour 20 minutes (direct)
- **Aircraft:** Airbus A320
- **Amenities:** Paid light meals/snacks; USB power (no free Wi-Fi); personal item only.
- **Price Breakdown (per adult):** Base fare ~$50 + taxes ~$20 (part of total itinerary).
- **Detailed Info:** Non-stop, economy seat pitch ~28–31 inches. No pre-assigned seats (select during check-in or pay extra). Baggage allowance: 1 personal item (max 15.7x9.8x7.9 inches, 15 lbs).

**Seat Map Summary (Economy Cabin - Main Deck, ~180 seats total):**
- Layout: 3-3 (A-B-C | D-E-F; A/C/D/F are window/aisle).
- Rows 1–5 shown (full map has ~30 rows; exit row 1 has extra legroom but restrictions—no stowing under seat).
- Availability: Most seats open; prices for selection: $28 (exit row premium) or $20 (standard).
- Example Seats:
  - Row 1 (Exit - Extra Legroom): 1A (window, $28), 1B (middle, $28), 1C (aisle, $28), 1D (aisle, $28), 1E (middle, $28).
  - Row 2: 2A (window, $20), 2B ($20), 2C (aisle, $20), 2D ($20), 2E ($20).
  - Rows 3–5: Similar to Row 2 ($20 each; all normal).
- Recommendation: Book window (A) or aisle (C/D) in rows 2–5 for comfort. Avoid middles (B/E) if possible.

#### Flight 2: Paris (ORY - Orly Airport) to Berlin (BER - Brandenburg Airport)
- **Date:** December 8, 2024 (after 1 week in Paris)
- **Flight Number:** U2 4873 (operated and marketed by EasyJet)
- **Departure:** 07:30 AM from ORY (Paris Orly, ~10 miles south of central Paris; easier access than CDG)
- **Arrival:** 09:15 AM at BER (Berlin Brandenburg, ~14 miles south of central Berlin; S-Bahn to city ~30 mins)
- **Duration:** 1 hour 45 minutes (direct)
- **Aircraft:** Airbus A320
- **Amenities:** Same as above—paid light meals; personal item only.
- **Price Breakdown (per adult):** Base fare ~$50 + taxes ~$18 (part of total).
- **Detailed Info:** Non-stop, standard economy. Transfer from CDG to ORY (~45 mins by taxi/RER; plan buffer time).

**Seat Map Summary (Economy Cabin - Main Deck):**
- Layout: Same 3-3 configuration.
- Rows 1–5 shown (similar to Flight 1).
- Availability: High; some seats pre-booked.
- Example Seats:
  - Row 1 (Exit): 1A (window, $29), 1B ($29), 1D (aisle, $29), 1E ($29). (1C unavailable.)
  - Row 2: 2A–2E all normal (~$25 each; some unpriced/available).
  - Rows 3–5: All normal ($25 each; full availability).
- Recommendation: Opt for Row 1 for legroom if your team needs space (extra fee applies). Aisle seats in rows 3–5 for easy access.

#### Flight 3: Berlin (BER) to London (LGW - Gatwick Airport)
- **Date:** December 15, 2024 (after 1 week in Berlin)
- **Flight Number:** U2 8628 (operated and marketed by EasyJet)
- **Departure:** 07:00 AM from BER
- **Arrival:** 08:05 AM at LGW (London Gatwick, ~30 miles south of central London; Gatwick Express train ~30 mins)
- **Duration:** 2 hours 5 minutes (direct)
- **Aircraft:** Airbus A320
- **Amenities:** Paid light meals; personal item only.
- **Price Breakdown (per adult):** Base fare ~$46 + taxes ~$18 (part of total).
- **Detailed Info:** Non-stop, economy. Early arrival in London allows full day.

**Seat Map Summary (Economy Cabin - Main Deck):**
- Layout: 3-3 (A-B-C | D-E-F).
- Rows 1–5 shown.
- Availability: Good; prices vary slightly.
- Example Seats:
  - Row 1 (Exit): All 1A–1E normal ($29 each; extra legroom).
  - Row 2: 2A–2C & 2E ($26 each); 2D normal/unpriced.
  - Rows 3–5: All normal ($26 each; high availability).
- Recommendation: Front rows (1–3) for quicker deplaning. Window seats for views over the Channel.

### Why This is the Best Option
- **Total Duration:** ~5 hours flying time (spread over dates); all direct flights minimize hassle.
- **Compared to Alternatives:** Cheapest option is identical at $202. Fastest is $519 but longer overall due to connections. This "BEST" pick has no layovers, low emissions, and morning flights (avoids peak pricing/delays).
